From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:54:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the USB2 PHY of the USB3
 controller

Add the node of the USB 2.0 PHY of the USB3 DRD controller. Its reset
comes from the SERDES CCU, its resistor calibration sits in the system
control block, which it reaches through the system control node.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the PHY node binds, and
the USB3 controller comes up through it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 3f3d90cd4041..66f3532a1954 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -740,6 +740,16 @@ dma: dma-controller@4601000 {
 			#dma-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		usb3_u2phy: phy@6b00000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-usb2-phy";
+			reg = <0x06b00000 0x800>;
+			allwinner,sram = <&syscon>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_RES_DCAP_24M>;
+			resets = <&serdes_ccu RST_USB3_USB2_PHY>;
+			#phy-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		serdes_ccu: clock-controller@6c00000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu";
 			reg = <0x06c00000 0x10>;
